<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tettnang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tettnang is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, near the northern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a>, known for its hop growing. It was the residence of the Tettnang line of the counts of Montfort, who built its baroque New Palace in the 18th century. Deep in debt, the counts sold it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1780; it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1805 and to Württemberg in 1810.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tettnang.jpg" alt="Tettnang" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: -- Ingo2802 18:09, 26. Mai 2006 (CEST) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tettnang3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
